# Breaking changes to the standard library's public surface, declared.
#
# `scripts/check-compat.sh` refuses a removed, retyped or
# effect-widened public name unless a line here names it against the
# version that makes the change. That is the whole enforcement: a
# break is allowed, and it is allowed only when somebody wrote down
# that they meant it.
#
# Format, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <version>  <kind-letter>  <name>  <why>
#
# CLI and RUST rows record other interface breaks. AXSYM comparisons
# use the single-letter kinds.
#
# The kind letter is AXSYM's: F function, D data, C constructor,
# S struct, T trait, M macro. `docs/compatibility.md` is the policy
# this file implements.

