# wrappers answer `(Result Int Error)` instead of an Int that is a
# result when non-negative and a negated errno when negative.
#
# They read WIDENED rather than CHANGED because the effect row moved
# too: building an `Error` allocates, so each gained `Alloc`. The type
# changed as well - a widened row and a changed signature are the same
# event here, and the gate reports the coarser one.
