# `IO.cwd` answer `(Result String Error)` instead of a `String` that is
# the path when it worked and `""` when it did not.
#
# THESE ARE `CHANGED`, NOT `WIDENED`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THE
# SLICE EXISTS. Every earlier ERR-ADOPT-1 row gained `Alloc` because
# building an `Error` allocates. These two do not: measured before and
# after, `#effects=` is `Alloc,IO,Mut` either way, because the function
# already `memAlloc`s a 4097-byte buffer and `strDup`s its answer. It
# is the only remaining failure sentinel in `Sys.ax` that a caller pays
# nothing new for, which is what made it portable while `sysWriteFd`,
# `sysReadFd`, `netAccept`, `netAcceptFrom` and `netPollWait` - `IO`
# alone - stay excluded.
#
# A caller that wants the old behaviour writes `(unwrapOr <call> "")`,
# which is what both `self_host/lsp.ax` sites now say out loud.
